  "claim": "Scouting pass, no theorem activated. For UT3(F4) x| C3 the exact reduction is also approximation-preserving (one query and a known additive constant; Goldberg-Jerrum Thm. 1 at Q = 64 > 2), so approximating H_K(G) is #BIS-hard; this is folded into ROWELL-NOTE-20261026-001 as a proposition. For the Heisenberg groups the pure-leaf recipe is exact but not approximation-preserving, because the psi^-1 sector is never steered and stays maximal; a two-sided repair is sketched for r in {3, 4}. For S4 there is no verdict: the knot reduction interpolates, the link reduction is planar ferromagnetic Potts, and every tripled series-parallel gadget leaves equal states unpenalized. Kernel-count interactions are positive semidefinite. Interest 1/3 as a standalone epic.",
